The prev variable is our output, and keeps track of the reversed portion. Current is the linked list we start with.
Our while loop condition ensures that the loop doesn't break until the current list has nothing left inside, as by then everything will be in prev.
First, we start by saving the next node in the current sequence, which is 7.
Then, we make the 4 lead into None instead of 7.
Next, we make prev point to the same line of 4 to None as current does, then we reassign current to whatever's left.
We repeat these steps three times, until the node current is reversed into the node prev.
We then return prev to complete the problem.
